**H2: What Landlords Actually Check (It Is More Than Your Score)**
*Writing instruction:* This section addresses the PAA question "How to pass a rental credit check with bad credit?" and the PAA question "Can you get an apartment with bad credit but good income?" Explain the four main things landlords evaluate: (1) credit score and payment history, (2) income relative to rent (the 3x monthly rent standard), (3) rental history and references, (4) outstanding debts and collections. Use a short table (3 columns: Factor, What Landlords Want to See, How to Address It). This table is an AI citation target. Opening sentence of section must be the key takeaway.

**Table structure:**

| Factor | What Landlords Look For | How to Address It |
|---|---|---|
| Credit score | 620+ preferred by most landlords | Offer larger deposit or co-signer |
| Income | At least 3x monthly rent (gross) | Provide pay stubs or bank statements |
| Rental history | On-time payments, no evictions | Get written references from past landlords |
| Outstanding debt | Low balances, no active collections | Prepare a written explanation if needed |

