**H2: 6 Strategies That Work When Your Credit Score Is Low**
*Writing instruction:* This is the core how-to section. Present 6 numbered strategies in priority order (most accessible/highest impact first). Each strategy gets one short declarative headline, 2-3 sentences of explanation, and one specific action to take. No padding. No repeating what was said in the landlord-check section. Strategies should be:

1. Target private landlords instead of corporate complexes
2. Offer a larger security deposit (note: check state deposit caps before offering; California caps at 2 months, many states have no cap)
3. Show proof of income first, before they ask
4. Write a short letter explaining your credit history
5. Bring a co-signer or look into guarantor services
6. Apply to properties with vacancies that have been sitting

*Writing instruction continued:* Do not use passive voice. Every sentence should tell the reader what to do or what to expect. Example of correct tone: "Call the landlord before applying. Explain your income and offer a larger deposit upfront. Many private owners will give you a hearing that a corporate leasing office never would."

